6373862 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143139" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373862 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373862 #edb/ref 1071 "At each point $P$ on a particular curve, the derivative ${y}^{′}(x)$ is proportional to the shortest distance from $P$ to the $y$-axis. The derivative at the point $(3,-5)$ equals $24.$ What differential equation describes this curve?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373862 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e6b89f7e-afce-55f3-8c93-dbf9b7119d01" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373862 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*At each point $P$ on a particular curve, the **derivative** ${y}^{′}(x)$ is **proportional** to the **shortest distance from $P$ to the $y$-axis**.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The *shortest distance from $P$ to the $y$-axis* is given by $|x|.$\n\n- Since the *derivative* is *proportional to* the shortest distance from $P$ to the $y$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)=k\\cdot |x|\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant.\n\nSo, our differential equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)=k|x|.\n$$\n\nIn addition, we're told that ${y}^{′}(x)=24$ when at the point $(3,-5).$ We can use this to determine the value of the coefficient $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24=k|3|\\,⟹\\,k=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the differential equation describing the curve is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)=8|x|.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373863 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373863 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373863 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373866 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373863 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373863 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373863 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373863 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373863 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17